Recent analyses of lepton flavor universality (LFU) violating decays have suggested that new physics beyond the Standard Model might exist, potentially influencing multiple areas. To gain insights into these potential effects, we have conducted a comprehensive study of the lepton flavor universality violating decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ within the context of a theoretical model called $U_1$ leptoquark. By leveraging recent data on $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ decay, we have derived stringent constraints on the $U_1$ leptoquark at energy scales of several TeV. Furthermore, we have predicted branching ratios for $\Lambda_b 	o p  ar{
u}_	au$ decays, highlighting the potential for these processes to be experimentally observed.
